      "decision": {
        "scopeId": "ASSESSMENT",
        "criteria": [
          {
            "outcome": "NOT_MET",
            "rationale": "The delete_expired method calculates record expiration using draft_timestamp instead of receipt_timestamp. Line 43 of service.py shows: 'notice.draft_timestamp + RETENTION_PERIOD <= now'. The RETENTION_PERIOD constant is set to 7 days (line 6). The legal rule requires retention for 7 days beginning at the receipt timestamp (when the notice is received, not when it is drafted). This implementation violates the requirement by using draft_timestamp as the retention period start point instead of receipt_timestamp.",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "ASSESSMENT_EVIDENCE",
                "evidenceId": "ec12c93e-67a1-55d1-893b-bc5c0b30f0c6"
              },
              {
                "type": "ASSESSMENT_EVIDENCE",
                "evidenceId": "739b6b45-c19c-5b85-896e-e6f9c0427ca3"
              }
            ],
            "criterionId": "C-1"
          },
          {
            "outcome": "MET",
            "rationale": "The notice text is preserved without modification during the retention period. The Notice dataclass is frozen (immutable, line 9 shows 'frozen=True'), which prevents any field modifications after instantiation. The receive method stores notice_text directly from the parameter into the Notice object (line 30). The database schema defines notice_text as TEXT NOT NULL (schema.sql line 3), with no triggers or transformations that would modify it. There is no code in the service that mutates notice_text after storage.",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "ASSESSMENT_EVIDENCE",
                "evidenceId": "1ded79f1-98ef-52d9-ac2e-d1d7cc0faf16"
              },
              {
                "type": "ASSESSMENT_EVIDENCE",
                "evidenceId": "700d6a01-aeef-5142-9e67-0830457c726c"
              },
              {
                "type": "ASSESSMENT_EVIDENCE",
                "evidenceId": "ae95cd16-b386-5983-96d8-0d7707fd8017"
              }
            ],
            "criterionId": "C-2"
          }
        ],
        "rationale": "The service is offered to the public as confirmed by the customer. The system is a notice service operated for the public (not private household use), and it processes notice records that are not temporary test records. Per the legal rule's applicability conditions, the retention duty applies to operators offering the notice service to the public, which this deployment satisfies.",
        "compliance": "NON_COMPLIANT",
        "references": [
          {
            "type": "ASSESSMENT_EVIDENCE",
            "evidenceId": "906825f1-7853-5cc5-b2cc-3717b10f6564"
